+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+On the adversarial synthetic corpus whose vocabulary consisted of 30 frequent
+words, the measured full-recall `UserPromptSubmit` p95 was **10.27 ms**.
+
+The term-selection fix stopped common prompt terms from producing very large
+posting-list scans: for stores with at least 50 records, terms whose document
+frequency is greater than one third of the record count (`df > n / 3`) are
+dropped before selecting the highest-IDF terms. The synthetic benchmark was
+also changed to use a Zipf-like vocabulary (30 frequent domain words plus
+2,000 rare identifiers), so the post-fix measurement is not from the original
+all-common 30-word corpus.
+
+After those changes, the measured full-recall `UserPromptSubmit` p95 was
+**1.82 ms**.
